A||||3||Bens88GT||How do you adjust the TV cable?||||5||
Z||000000||Bens88GT||02-11-2000||03:17 PM||||I have an automatic, and I have to push the gas pedal ALL the way to the floor before the engine goes to wide-open throttle and the tranny waits to shift until 5500 rpm. I want to make the gas pedal more responsive, so I don't have to push it nearly as far to get WOT. Would adjusting the Throttle-Valve cable accomplish this? If so, where is it located and how do I do it?<P>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula||02-11-2000||08:52 PM||||its on the thing that says HOLLEY by the big red thing that says fiero. it is on the top of the "holley" thing.  there should be a screw to adjust it AND yes it will change your response.<P>I played with mine to the point that I couldn't push the gas pedal down.<P>keeps it under the speed limit LOL||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bens88GT||02-12-2000||12:17 AM||||Hey Formula, thanks for the information! This'll make the little GT more fun.<P>-Ben||||reg||10
Z||000003||daved||02-12-2000||12:22 AM||||Here in Canada it's illegal to mess with your TV cable...you have to call Rogers Cable LOL!<BR>Sounds to me as if the response you get is as it was designed. WOT is when you have your foot to the floor. The TV cable does, however , control the shift point, which I think is what you are after. My adjuster is broken, so I just pulled out a 1/2" or so of the inner wire, and clamped it in place with the innards of an electrical "Marr" connector. It will take some experimentation to find the correct point.||||reg||1
